+--------+
|Soft Serve|
+--------+

Soft Serve stores all of its state below /var/db/soft-serve: the Git
repositories, the SQLite database, the SSH host and client keys and the
configuration file.  The rc.d(8) script starts the server as the
_softserve user with /var/db/soft-serve as the working directory.

The rc.d(8) script disables the unauthenticated git:// daemon and the
stats endpoint and binds the HTTP interface to localhost.  The SSH
listener remains enabled on port 23231 on all interfaces.

Initial setup:

	doas rcctl enable soft_serve
	doas rcctl start soft_serve

The first SSH client to connect and choose a username becomes the
administrator:

	ssh -p 23231 localhost

For non-interactive provisioning, add an SSH public key to
SOFT_SERVE_INITIAL_ADMIN_KEYS in the rc_start() environment before the
first start, or import keys later with:

	doas -u _softserve soft admin user create \
		--username admin --admin \
		--public-key "$(cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub)"

Listener configuration is read from /var/db/soft-serve/config.yaml.
The default configuration enables the SSH server (:23231), the git
daemon (:9418), the HTTP server (:23232) and the stats endpoint
(localhost:23233); the rc.d(8) environment above overrides the git,
HTTP and stats settings.

The generated configuration file is owned by _softserve and is not
managed by the package: it is preserved across upgrades.
